{"author":{"id":"1d5f412cdeafe9987ad9876b0995bf5032718543d34c038a50cdb41808e9874c"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788305207,"nonce":"ccc7tb2cDaJ0E5thAnQfP4JOMmo=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOULVc1M8AAAABPPiH2A","github-url":"https://github.com/kanya-approve/torram-ng/issues/24","origin":"github"},"title":"Filesystem walk tests membership against a list instead of a set","message":"```python\nsizes = get_file_sizes(info)          # a list\n...\nif filesize in sizes:                 # O(len(sizes)) per file on disk\n    filesizes.setdefault(filesize, []).append(filepath)\n```\n\n`sizes` is a list, so this is a linear scan for every file encountered during the walk, making discovery O(files_on_disk x files_in_torrent).\n\nScanning a drive holding a million files against a torrent of ten thousand is 1e10 comparisons just to decide which files are worth looking at.\n\nA `set` makes it O(1). `os.scandir()` also avoids a second `stat` syscall per entry, since `DirEntry` carries the size already on most platforms.","files":null}]}